"prose": [
{
"from": 227,
"to": 229,
"text": "The gates are the standing lint, unit and default-selection entries; one count entry that reads the lift; the self-test and the two graded verbs of the chunk's instrument; the preservation guard; two readers of the records the steps leave; the harness smoke with G2 and G4 over its home; the native `pre-push`; and the operator's hygiene, push and CI read."
},
{
"from": 231,
"to": 234,
"text": "No entry is a mutation run and no entry is a live leg (`inputs#I1`). The score and the three witness runs are one-shot measurements driven by steps 2 and 14; their records are in `evidence/`, and the two reader entries assert those records. A reader writes nothing, so neither carries an `artifact` key. The witness run is also each new kill case's remove-the-guard reading: its mutant is the guard neutralised and `caught` is the test red."
},
{
"from": 236,
"to": 237,
"text": "The count entry and the preservation guard read against the base commit, because the operator pass's pre-CI commit moves HEAD onto the chunk. The guard lists no file a step edits."
},
{
"from": 239,
"to": 243,
"text": "The two graded instrument entries need the audit's tools on the host (`jscpd` 5.0.16, `rust-code-analysis-cli` 0.0.25, both read present at P3); they run at /implement and at the wrap's light gate on the dev host, not in CI. The instrument's known-verdict controls are its listed `selftest`, ahead of them. `evidence/scalars.md`, `evidence/e2e-score.md` and `evidence/survivors.md` have no listed producer: each is written by hand at its step from what a run printed."
}
],
